  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nWhile the majority of the area is expected to remain dry, some light \ndrizzle could materialize over the northeast mountains as a cold \nfront crosses the area this morning. High pressure quickly regains \ncontrol behind the front and allows quiet weather to persist into \nthe weekend.\n\nMild temperatures, coupled with dewpoints in the 30s to 40s, should \nresult in minimum relative humidity values ranging from 25-35% \nacross much of the area this afternoon, and likely Saturday \nafternoon as well. That being said, light winds should alleviate \nfire weather concerns for this week.\n\nA shortwave approaches the area this weekend; however, the forecast \nhas been trending drier in response to a slower eastward retreat of \nlow-level high pressure. Some precipitation could eventually \ninfringe upon the western half of the forecast area late Sunday into \nMonday, but widespread precipitation chances are more likely to hold \noff until an upper trough and low track into the Middle Ohio Valley \nmid to late week next week.",
